- # KnowMine — AI-Native Personal Knowledge Base
- > Give your AI agent long-term memory with semantic vector search.
- KnowMine is a personal knowledge management system built for AI agents. Unlike file-based or keyword-search tools, KnowMine uses **pgvector semantic search** to find knowledge by meaning, not just keywords. Every entry is automatically vectorized, tagged, and organized — your agent builds a growing knowledge graph it can query at any time.
- **KnowMine 是一个为 AI Agent 构建的个人知识库，支持语义向量检索、AI 洞察、知识关联发现。**
- ## Why KnowMine?
- - **Semantic vector search (pgvector)** — find knowledge by meaning, not keywords. Ask "what did I learn about pricing strategy?" and get relevant results even if those exact words were never used.
- - **11 MCP tools** — full CRUD + semantic search + AI insights + memory system, all via standard MCP protocol.
- - **Automatic knowledge association** — discover hidden connections between entries through vector similarity.
- - **AI-generated user profile (Soul)** — export a portable system prompt that captures your preferences, decisions, and expertise for use in any AI platform.
- - **Zero-friction capture** — save notes, insights, dev logs, articles, and reflections with automatic title extraction, tagging, and folder assignment.
- ## Quick Start
- ### 1. Get your MCP key
- Sign up at [knowmine.ai](https://knowmine.ai) and copy your MCP API key from settings.
- ### 2. Connect to your agent
- This is a **remote-hosted** MCP server — no Docker or local install needed.
- For OpenClaw, install via ClawHub:
- ### 3. Start building your knowledge
- Your agent can now read and write to your personal knowledge base.
- ## Available Tools (11)
- ### Knowledge Management
- | Tool | Description |
- | Tool | Description |
- | Tool | Description |
- | `add_knowledge` | Save a knowledge entry (note, insight, dev_log, article, reflection). AI auto-extracts title, tags, and assigns to folders. Content is automatically vectorized. |
- | `search_my_knowledge` | Semantic vector search across your entire knowledge base. Supports filtering by type and tags. Returns results ranked by similarity. |
- | `get_knowledge` | Retrieve full content of a single entry by ID. |
- | `update_knowledge` | Update title, content, type, or tags. Content changes trigger automatic re-vectorization. |
- | `delete_knowledge` | Remove an entry permanently. |
- | `get_related_knowledge` | Discover hidden connections — find entries related to a given entry via vector similarity. |
- | `list_folders` | Browse your knowledge structure and see recent entries per folder. |
- ### Memory System
- | `save_memory` | Persist decisions, lessons, insights, preferences, and domain knowledge from conversations. Supports cross-platform memory (Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, etc). |
- | `recall_memory` | Search past memories with natural language. Filter by type (decision, insight, lesson, preference, domain_knowledge). |
- ### AI Intelligence
- | `get_soul` | Generate an AI user profile based on your accumulated knowledge. Export as a system prompt portable to any AI platform. |
- | `get_insight` | AI-powered analysis of your knowledge — frequent topics, thinking patterns, cross-time correlations. |
- ## How It's Different
- | Feature | KnowMine | File-based tools | Keyword search tools |
- |---------|----------|-------------------|---------------------|
- | Search method | pgvector semantic similarity | File path / grep | Exact keyword match |
- | Auto-organization | AI tags, titles, folders | Manual | Manual |
- | Knowledge discovery | Vector association networks | None | None |
- | Cross-platform memory | Soul export as system prompt | None | None |
- | MCP protocol | 11 standard tools | Varies | Varies |
- | Data persistence | Cloud (PostgreSQL) | Local files | Varies |
- ## Use When...
- - You need to **remember context across conversations** — save key decisions, insights, and lessons so future sessions start informed.
- - You want to **search your personal knowledge semantically** — "what did I decide about database architecture?" finds relevant entries even without exact keyword matches.
- - You're **switching between AI platforms** — export your Soul as a system prompt to carry context from Claude to GPT to Gemini.
- - You want to **discover connections** in your knowledge — `get_related_knowledge` reveals surprising links between entries you didn't know were related.
- - You need **persistent memory for your agent** — build a growing knowledge base that gets smarter over time.
- ## Example Workflows
- **Research Assistant:**
- 1. save_memory: "Decided to use Rust for the CLI — performance critical, single binary deploy"
- 2. add_knowledge: Save a detailed comparison of Rust vs Go for CLI tools
- 3. Later: search_my_knowledge("CLI language decision") → finds both the decision and the comparison
- 4. get_related_knowledge → discovers your earlier notes about deployment strategies are related
- **Cross-Session Context:**
- 1. End of session: save_memory with key decisions and open questions
- 2. New session: recall_memory("what was I working on?") → instant context recovery
- 3. get_soul → paste into any AI platform for full personality + preference context
- ## Data Security
- - Each API key is bound to one user account — full data isolation
- - API keys stored as SHA-256 hashes, plaintext never persisted server-side
- - Rate limited: 60 requests/minute
- ## Technical Details
- - **Vector engine**: pgvector on PostgreSQL (Neon)
- - **Embedding model**: OpenAI `text-embedding-3-small`
- - **Protocol**: MCP (Model Context Protocol) over Streamable HTTP
- - **Auth**: API key via Bearer token or query parameter
- - **Data format**: Markdown content with structured metadata
